\section{Supermassive Black Hole Growth}

Black holes act as informational sinks. The growth law is:
\begin{equation}
\dot{M}_{\rm BH} = \gamma\,\rho_I\,A_0(1+\delta),
\end{equation}
where $\gamma$ is the conversion coefficient, $A_0$ the baseline capture area,
and $\delta$ the chaotic inflow amplification factor.

The integrated mass is:
\begin{equation}
M_{\rm BH}(t) = M_{\rm seed} 
+ \gamma A_0 (1+\delta) \int_{t_0}^{t} \rho_I(t')\,dt'.
\end{equation}